  <h1>Lesson 36: To-Do List - Your Daily Task App</h1>
  <p>Add, Complete, Delete, Filter, Save - Like Real Apps | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What Will We Build?</h2>
    <p>Today we build a <b>real To-Do List app</b> - Just like Google Tasks. You can add a task, mark it as done, delete it, filter All / Active / Done, and your tasks are saved in LocalStorage - Even after refresh, they stay.</p>
    <p>This project uses: <b>Array of Objects</b> for tasks, <b>Functions</b> for add/delete/toggle, <b>DOM</b> to show tasks, <b>Events</b> for clicks, <b>LocalStorage</b> to save, <b>Loop</b> to show all tasks.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>How It Works - Data First:</b> We do NOT save HTML. We save DATA - An array like <code>[{ text: "Buy milk", done: false }, { text: "Study JS", done: true }]</code>. Then a function <code>showTasks()</code> reads this array and creates HTML for it. Change data - Call showTasks() - Page updates. This is how all real apps work.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Try Your To-Do App</h2>
    <p>Add tasks, tick them done, delete them, try filters. Then refresh - Tasks will still be there:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div class="todo-wrap">
        <h3 style="text-align:center;margin:0">✅ My To-Do List</h3>
        <p id="todoCount" style="text-align:center;color:#64748b;font-size:13px;margin:6px 0">0 tasks - 0 done</p>
        <div class="progress"><div class="progress-bar" id="todoProgress"></div></div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px">
          <input class="demo-input" id="todoInput" type="text" placeholder="Type task - e.g. Study JavaScript" onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter') addTodo()">
          <button class="btn btn-js" style="margin:0;white-space:nowrap" onclick="addTodo()">Add ➕</button>
        </div>
        <div class="filter-row">
          <button class="filter-btn active" id="filterAll" onclick="setFilter('all')">All</button>
          <button class="filter-btn" id="filterActive" onclick="setFilter('active')">Active</button>
          <button class="filter-btn" id="filterDone" onclick="setFilter('done')">Done</button>
        </div>
        <div id="todoList"></div>
        <button class="btn" style="width:100%;background:#dc2626" onclick="clearDone()">Clear Completed 🧹</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Step 1 - Data - Array of Objects</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let todos = [</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ text: "Buy milk", done: false },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ text: "Study JavaScript", done: false },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ text: "Walk 30 min", done: true }</span><br>
<span class="text">];</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Each task is an object - text = What to do, done = Is it finished?</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>4. Step 2 - showTasks() - Data to HTML</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function showTasks() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let list = document.getElementById("todoList");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">list.innerHTML = ""; // Clear old HTML</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < todos.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let t = todos[i];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let checked = t.done ? "checked" : "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let style = t.done ? "text-decoration:line-through" : "";</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">list.innerHTML += `</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;input type="checkbox" ${checked} onclick="toggleTask(${i})"&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;span style="${style}"&gt;${t.text}&lt;/span&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;button onclick="deleteTask(${i})"&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;/div&gt;`;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("todos", JSON.stringify(todos)); // Save</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Key Idea:</b> Notice <code>onclick="toggleTask(${i})"</code> - We pass the index number. So when you click task 2, JavaScript knows "Toggle task number 2".</p>
    <h2>5. Step 3 - Add, Toggle, Delete - 3 Small Functions</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// ADD - Take input, push to array, show again</span><br>
<span class="text">function addTodo() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let input = document.getElementById("todoInput");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let text = input.value.trim();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (text === "") { alert("Please type a task!"); return; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">todos.push({ text: text, done: false });</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">input.value = "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showTasks();</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// TOGGLE - Done to Not Done, Not Done to Done</span><br>
<span class="text">function toggleTask(index) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">todos[index].done = !todos[index].done; // Flip true/false</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showTasks();</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// DELETE - Remove one task by index</span><br>
<span class="text">function deleteTask(index) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">todos.splice(index, 1); // Remove 1 item at index</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">showTasks();</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. What is splice()?</h2>
    <p><b>splice(index, howMany)</b> = Remove items from array at a position.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana", "Mango", "Grapes"];</span><br>
<span class="text">fruits.splice(1, 1); // Remove 1 item at index 1 - Banana removed</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits); // ["Apple", "Mango", "Grapes"]</span><br><br>
<span class="text">fruits.splice(0, 2); // Remove 2 items from start</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(fruits); // ["Grapes"]</span>
    </code></div>
    <p>Difference: <code>pop()</code> only removes last item. <code>splice()</code> can remove any item by index - Perfect for delete button.</p>
    <h2>7. Complete Example - Mini To-Do in 30 Lines</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">My Tasks</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"task"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"New task"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"addTodo()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Add</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"list"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let todos = [];</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function showTasks() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let html = "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < todos.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">html += "&lt;p&gt;" + todos[i].text + " &lt;button onclick='deleteTask(" + i + ")'&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/p&gt;";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("list").innerHTML = html;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function addTodo() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let t = document.getElementById("task").value.trim();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (t !== "") { todos.push({ text: t, done: false }); document.getElementById("task").value = ""; showTasks(); }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function deleteTask(i) { todos.splice(i, 1); showTasks(); }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Homework - Make It Better</h2>
    <p>In Playground, add these to your To-Do:</p>
    <p>1. Full To-Do like demo - Add, Toggle, Delete, Filter All / Active / Done<br>2. LocalStorage Save - On load, read saved todos with JSON.parse, on every change save with JSON.stringify<br>3. Edit Button - Click Edit, change task text with prompt() and save</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Data First - Array of objects { text, done } | showTasks() = Array to HTML, call after every change | add = push({ text, done: false }) | toggle = todos[i].done = !todos[i].done | delete = splice(index, 1) | Save = JSON.stringify + setItem | Load = JSON.parse + getItem | Filter = Show only done / not done / all</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson37">Lesson 37 - Quiz App</a> - Build a quiz with questions, timer, score, and result screen.</p>
